00:22:34,933 --> 00:22:36,600
哎，真倒霉！
Oh, bother!

401
00:22:38,833 --> 00:22:40,267
（引擎轰鸣）
(ENGINES ROARING)

402
00:22:43,867 --> 00:22:45,367
就这么结束了。
And that was that.

403
00:22:45,400 --> 00:22:47,967
这是我对这台
传奇引擎致以的敬意。
My tribute to
an amazing engine.

404
00:22:51,167 --> 00:22:53,767
实在抱歉，
我已经拼尽全力了，
I'm sorry,
it was the best I could do,

405
00:22:53,800 --> 00:22:57,900
但无论如何都要感谢你
长达37年的忠诚服役。
but thanks anyway,
for the 37 years of service.

406
00:23:00,067 --> 00:23:01,400
-克拉克森：真是台神机。
-确实。
-CLARKSON: Great engine.
-Yeah.

407
00:23:01,433 --> 00:23:04,067
而且我必须得说，
这话我一定要说，
And I must say,
I have to say this,

408
00:23:04,167 --> 00:23:05,667
-你开得真是太棒了。
-谢谢。
-a great drive from you.
-Thank you.

409
00:23:05,700 --> 00:23:08,967
确实很棒。
不过媒体可就没这么客气了，
我得承认。
It really was.
The press were less kind,
I must admit.

410
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:13,167
我这儿有一份剪报，
“《Top Gear》主持人
在斯内特顿赛道苦苦挣扎”。
I've got a cutting here,
Top Gear presenter
struggles at Snetterton.

411
00:23:13,200 --> 00:23:15,500
这简直太不公平了！
这根本不公道。
That is just so unfair!
That is unfair.

412
00:23:15,533 --> 00:23:18,467
你瞧瞧别人的车，
过弯时车身平平稳稳，
而我的车歪得不行，
You saw the other cars,
they were cornering level,
and mine was leaning,

413
00:23:18,500 --> 00:23:21,800
因为我用的只是
原厂普通悬挂
和普通刹车，
because I only had
ordinary suspension
and ordinary brakes

414
00:23:21,833 --> 00:23:25,267
而且发动机马力
也根本比不上
其他人的车。
and the engine
wasn't as powerful
as everyone else's.

415
00:23:25,300 --> 00:23:26,833
要不要我
帮你找个台阶下？
You want me to
get you out of this hole?

416
00:23:26,867 --> 00:23:28,233
-求之不得，赶紧的。
-（观众笑声）
-Yes, please.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

417
00:23:28,267 --> 00:23:30,167
-那我们来见见嘉宾？
-好啊，有请。
-Shall we meet a guest?
-Yes, please.

418
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:35,567
好了，今晚开廉价车的
明星嘉宾，
长了一对硕大无比的耳朵。
Okay, our star in
the Reasonably Priced Car
tonight has very big ears.

419
00:23:35,600 --> 00:23:37,000
呃，实际上大到什么程度呢，
Uh, so big, in fact,

420
00:23:37,033 --> 00:23:38,433
要是车轮子
再掉一次的话，
that if the wheel
comes off again,

421
00:23:38,467 --> 00:23:41,000
他完全可以用这对耳朵
当空气减速板用。
he will be able to
use them as air-brakes.

422
00:23:41,033 --> 00:23:43,400
女士们先生们，
马丁·克鲁尼斯！
Ladies and gentlemen,
Martin Clunes.

423
00:23:43,433 --> 00:23:44,667
（观众欢呼）
(AUDIENCE CHEERING)

424
00:23:45,933 --> 00:23:47,400
-你好！
-非常感谢。
-Hello!
-Thank you very much.

425
00:23:47,433 --> 00:23:49,567
-谢谢，谢谢大家。
-请坐。
-Thank you. Thank you.
-Have a seat.

426
00:23:53,567 --> 00:23:54,667
嗯……
Um...

427
00:23:55,733 --> 00:23:57,767
那么，呃……
Now, um...

428
00:23:57,800 --> 00:23:59,733
-真是热烈非凡的欢迎。
-是啊，挺带劲的，对吧？
-A rapturous welcome.
-Yeah. Not bad, was it?

429
00:23:59,767 --> 00:24:02,500
呃，话说，你看
上周那期节目了吗？
Um, now, did you
see the show
last week

430
00:24:02,533 --> 00:24:04,200
就是轮子飞掉的那期？
when the wheel fell off?

431
00:24:04,233 --> 00:24:05,767
没看，
不过我听说了。
No, I didn't,
but I've heard about it.

432
00:24:05,800 --> 00:24:07,833
在我上车之前
他们就跟我打预防针了。
They told me about it
before I got in the car.

433
00:24:07,867 --> 00:24:10,000
-他们说这车的轮子掉过。
-这让你紧张了吗？
-They said the wheel
has come off.
-Did that make you nervous?

434
00:24:10,033 --> 00:24:11,467
没，反正我本来就很紧张。
No, I was already nervous.

435
00:24:11,500 --> 00:24:12,800
-你想亲眼看看吗？
-想啊，说实话我还真挺想看的。
-Would you like to see it?
-Yeah, I'd love to, actually.

436
00:24:12,833 --> 00:24:16,033
这就是上周
莱昂纳尔·里奇开的那次。
This is the one with
Lionel Richie last week.

437
00:24:16,067 --> 00:24:17,400
瞧这儿，下手有点狠。
Here he is, a bit brutal.

438
00:24:17,433 --> 00:24:19,767
-（克鲁尼斯轻笑）
-接着轮子就飞出去了。
-(CLUNES CHUCKLING)
-And there goes the wheel.

439
00:24:19,800 --> 00:24:21,167
轮子现在反超他了。
It's now overtaking him.

440
00:24:21,167 --> 00:24:22,167
（观众笑声）
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

441
00:24:22,200 --> 00:24:24,400
他冲出去了。
And off he goes.

442
00:24:24,433 --> 00:24:25,800
# 你好 #
# Hello #

443
00:24:25,833 --> 00:24:27,833
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

444
00:24:27,867 --> 00:24:29,633
刚才他差点就直接
在天花板上跳起舞来了。
He was so nearly dancing
on the ceiling, there.

445
00:24:29,667 --> 00:24:31,700
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

446
00:24:31,733 --> 00:24:35,633
聊聊你的汽车史吧，
呃，最初是从哪辆车开始的？
Now, your car history,
um, where does that begin?

447
00:24:35,667 --> 00:24:39,667
是从一辆希尔曼Minx开始的，
那车刚好够你
从温布尔登开到普特尼。
It started with a Hillman Minx
that would get you
from Wimbledon to Putney.

448
00:24:39,700 --> 00:24:41,033
有次它还被人给偷了，
And it once got stolen
by somebody,

449
00:24:41,067 --> 00:24:42,367
结果小偷最远
也就开到了普特尼，
but they only got
as far as Putney,

450
00:24:42,400 --> 00:24:44,167
因为这破车
最远也就只能跑这么远。
'cause that was
as far as it would go.

451
00:24:44,167 --> 00:24:46,233
我们还得
把水箱水给重新加满。
We had to
fill the radiator back.

452
00:24:46,267 --> 00:24:49,267
不过我找着了它，
又给顺了回来，
顺顺利利开回了家。
But I found it
and nicked it back
and got it home.

453
00:24:49,300 --> 00:24:51,900
严格来说，
偷自己的车
可不算偷。
Technically,
that's not stealing
if it's your own car.

454
00:24:51,933 --> 00:24:53,000
确实，没错。
That's true. Yeah.

455
00:24:53,033 --> 00:24:54,600
后来你去当了个跑龙套的……
Then you got
the bit part actor...

456
00:24:54,633 --> 00:24:57,833
你在《神秘博士》里
跑过龙套。
You were a bit part actor
in Doctor Who.

457
00:24:57,867 --> 00:24:59,800
其实我的戏份相当多好不好。
I had quite a big part,
actually.

458
00:24:59,833 --> 00:25:01,533
谢谢，没错，
我演的是特邀大反派。
Thank you, yes,
I was guest baddie.

459
00:25:01,567 --> 00:25:06,167
嗯，演完那个之后，
我就买了辆
3.0排量的宝马玩意儿。
Um, yes I did,
and then I bought
a BMW 3-litre thing.

460
00:25:06,200 --> 00:25:08,567
-哦，太棒了，挺好。
-在7系出来之前的那款。
-Oh, great. Good.
-Before the 7 Series.

461
00:25:08,600 --> 00:25:10,433
不过说真的，你确实得买辆好车，
Thing is though you needed
to buy a good car,

462
00:25:10,467 --> 00:25:14,133
因为很不幸，
我们手里正好有一张照片，
because we've actually got
a photograph,
I'm afraid to say,

463
00:25:14,167 --> 00:25:16,433
是你在《神秘博士》里的剧照，瞧，就是这张。
of you in Doctor Who,
there it is.

464
00:25:16,467 --> 00:25:18,300
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

465
00:25:18,333 --> 00:25:20,633
那年头的致幻蘑菇可真够劲啊。
Mushrooms were mushrooms
in those days.

466
00:25:21,567 --> 00:25:23,200
克拉克森：噢，瞧瞧那副德行！
CLARKSON: Ooh, look at that!

467
00:25:24,400 --> 00:25:26,100
自从拍完《邋遢男人》之后，
Now, since the days
of Men Behaving Badly,

468
00:25:26,133 --> 00:25:30,100
你就离开了伦敦，
搬去过清静日子了，算是吧。
you've left London
and moved to
the quiet life, really.

469
00:25:30,133 --> 00:25:31,800
嗯。
Mmm.

470
00:25:31,833 --> 00:25:33,433
怎么说呢，我听说你大半时间
都在搞木工活。
Why, I understand
you spend most of your life
doing carpentry.

471
00:25:33,467 --> 00:25:36,300
我确实干了不少木工活，是的。
是啊，我挺喜欢的。
I do do a fair bit
of carpentry, yeah.
Yeah, I do like it.

472
00:25:36,333 --> 00:25:37,367
图什么呢？
Why?

473
00:25:37,400 --> 00:25:39,000
图什么？
Why?

474
00:25:39,033 --> 00:25:42,433
因为我的本职工作，
基本就是穿上戏服、当小丑瞎折腾。
Because I basically,
dress up and prat around
for a living.

475
00:25:42,467 --> 00:25:45,900
然后这玩意儿顺着无线电波
被喷进千家万户的电视机里，
That then gets squirted
through the airwaves
to people's television sets,

476
00:25:45,933 --> 00:25:49,133
到头来你的辛勤劳动
几乎留不下任何实质成果。
and you're sort of
left with very little result
for your labour.

477
00:25:49,167 --> 00:25:52,100
所以能亲自去敲敲打打、
乒乒乓乓做点实物，感觉其实挺爽的，
So, it's actually quite good
to go and bang
and hammer something,

478
00:25:52,133 --> 00:25:55,533
忙活一整天下来，
起码还能落下一小块木头。
and at the end of the day,
have a tiny bit of wood left.

479
00:25:55,567 --> 00:25:57,133
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

480
00:25:59,700 --> 00:26:01,067
瞧瞧这个！
Look at that!

481
00:26:01,100 --> 00:26:03,867
我刚开始弄的时候
才这么大一点！
It was this big
when I started!

482
00:26:03,900 --> 00:26:05,633
不过乡下生活
挺合你心意？
But life in the country
suits you well?

483
00:26:05,667 --> 00:26:07,400
-是啊，非常惬意。
-那合你的驾驶风格吗？
在那边开车？
-Yeah, very much.
-Does that suit your
driving style down there?

484
00:26:07,433 --> 00:26:10,167
挺合的……
我就是个开“陆地巨舰”大货车的
司机，
It suits...
I'm a land barge
van driver,

485
00:26:10,167 --> 00:26:12,233
视线正好能越过绿篱，
视野一览无余。
so I can see over the hedges
and everything.

486
00:26:12,267 --> 00:26:13,767
你有一辆Amazon。
You've got an Amazon.

487
00:26:13,800 --> 00:26:15,400
噢，我是有辆Amazon，
Oh, I've got an Amazon,

488
00:26:15,433 --> 00:26:17,300
没错，但我还有两辆露营车，
两辆大众。
yeah, but I've also got
two camper vans,
two Volkswagens.

489
00:26:17,333 --> 00:26:20,067
-露营车？
-呃其实，
严格来说不算。
-Camper vans?
-Well, actually,
that's not strictly true.

490
00:26:20,167 --> 00:26:24,867
一辆是1969年的Microbus，
后面就只有一排
后座。
One's a 1969 Microbus
with just one set
of backseats.

491
00:26:24,900 --> 00:26:29,533
另一辆是1977年的货运小面包，
我正慢慢翻新呢。
And the other was
a 1977 delivery van
which I'm slowly doing up.

492
00:26:29,567 --> 00:26:32,733
你们搞的那个史上最伟大车型榜单
放哪儿去了？
Where's that thing you've got
of all time greatest cars?

493
00:26:32,767 --> 00:26:35,733
因为那上面根本没有
大众厢型车。
Because there's no
Volkswagen vans on there.

494
00:26:35,767 --> 00:26:37,967
而且我……
你问问现场这帮观众……
And I...
You ask this audience...

495
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:39,633
哪怕随便绕两个熟人，
Through a couple of
degrees of separation,

496
00:26:39,667 --> 00:26:42,533
每个人这辈子都接触过
这种大众车。
everyone's had some exposure
to these vans in their lives.

497
00:26:42,567 --> 00:26:44,733
是啊，但它们评不上最伟大的“车”，
最根本的原因在于——
Yeah, but they can't be
the greatest car
on the basis that

498
00:26:44,767 --> 00:26:46,633
它们压根不是轿车，
它们其实是货车。
they're not cars,
they're actually vans.

499
00:26:46,667 --> 00:26:49,333
要是我们评选
史上最伟大的厢型小货车……
If we were to do
the greatest vans
of all time...

500
00:26:49,367 --> 00:26:50,433
噢！扯淡！
Oh! Bollocks!

501
00:26:51,333 --> 00:26:52,667
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

502
00:26:52,700 --> 00:26:54,000
行，我拿外套告辞！
I'll get me coat!

503
00:26:54,033 --> 00:26:56,233
你到底想问观众
什么问题？
You want to ask the audience
what exactly?

504
00:26:56,267 --> 00:26:57,667
-问他们有没有……
-举个手，
-Whether or not they...
-Hands up,

505
00:26:57,700 --> 00:27:01,033
谁曾经坐过或者开过
大众露营车？
who's had some experience
of a Volkswagen camper van?

506
00:27:01,067 --> 00:27:04,167
别害羞。噢，
朋友父母的车，
搭过顺风车……
Come on. Oh,
your friends' parents,
you went for a ride...

507
00:27:04,167 --> 00:27:05,767
-献出初吻？
-我倒挺好奇的，
-First snog?
-I'm quite interested,

508
00:27:05,800 --> 00:27:09,267
你在大众车里有过什么“经历”……对，就是你。
what experience did you have
in a Volks... Yeah.

509
00:27:09,300 --> 00:27:10,833
（女观众含糊不清地说话）
(WOMAN TALKS INDISTINCTLY)

510
00:27:10,867 --> 00:27:12,500
那纯粹就是去露营度假！
It's just a camping holiday!

511
00:27:12,533 --> 00:27:14,167
跟你脑子里想的那种“经历”
可完全不是一码事。
It's not exactly
the kind of experience
you were thinking of.

512
00:27:14,200 --> 00:27:15,833
好歹也是在车里待过嘛，
不是吗？
It's time in a vehicle,
isn't it?

513
00:27:15,867 --> 00:27:18,667
有谁在露营车里有过
什么刺激的经历吗？
Does anybody have
an interesting experience
in a camper van?

514
00:27:18,700 --> 00:27:20,400
噢，你刚才可没说
要“刺激”的。
Oh, you never said
interesting.

515
00:27:22,833 --> 00:27:24,533
那你现在开的
那些车呢？
What about the cars
you've got now?

516
00:27:24,567 --> 00:27:28,400
我买了辆宝马6系，
就是你在节目里
喷得一文不值的那款。
I've got the BMW 6 Series
you slagged off
on your programme.

517
00:27:30,167 --> 00:27:32,633
你到底对它有什么成见？
那可是我第一次用上车载导航，
What was your problem?
It's the first time
I've had sat nav,

518
00:27:32,667 --> 00:27:34,233
而你……
你凭什么嫌弃那导航？
and you...
Why didn't you like
the sat nav?

519
00:27:34,267 --> 00:27:36,067
因为宝马里的导航根本就是个摆设，
这就是原因。
Well, it doesn't work
in a BMW, that's why.

520
00:27:36,167 --> 00:27:40,033
比如它压根不知道A40公路，
完全当它不存在。
It has no clue, for instance,
about the A40,
doesn't know that exists.

521
00:27:40,067 --> 00:27:42,633
前几天我从牛津出发，
从牛津开去伦敦，
Well, I set off from Oxford
the other day,
Oxford to London,

522
00:27:42,667 --> 00:27:45,533
本该走M40高速回去，
当时开的不是宝马，
back to the M40,
not in a BMW,

523
00:27:45,567 --> 00:27:47,033
结果它非要把我往M1高速上引。
tries to steer me onto the M1.

524
00:27:47,067 --> 00:27:49,300
不过你开导航语音了吗？
她的声音？
Have you switched her on
though, her voice?

525
00:27:49,333 --> 00:27:50,600
桑迪。
Sandy.

526
00:27:50,633 --> 00:27:51,900
-她真叫这名字？
-我管她叫桑迪。
-Is that what she's called?
-I call her Sandy.

527
00:27:51,933 --> 00:27:54,800
噢，她可绝了。
“请向左转，顺便抚摸我的后背。”
Oh, she's great.
"Turn left, stroke my back."

528
00:27:54,833 --> 00:27:56,167
-真的假的？
-真的。
-Yeah?
-Yeah.

529
00:27:56,167 --> 00:27:59,300
“捏捏我的大腿。
请在允许掉头处掉头。”
"Squeeze my leg.
Make a legal U-turn."

530
00:27:59,333 --> 00:28:00,333
“把这玩意儿穿上。”
"Put these on."

531
00:28:00,367 --> 00:28:02,800
你这是在跟一个女人搞外遇啊，
You're having an affair
with a woman

532
00:28:02,833 --> 00:28:04,933
-而且她就住在你的仪表盘里。
-没错。
-who lives in your dashboard.
-Yes.

533
00:28:06,267 --> 00:28:08,400
天哪，我的老天爷！
这想想都瘆得慌。
Oh, Lordy, Lord!
It's quite scary.

534
00:28:08,433 --> 00:28:10,833
不过你难道不觉得那车坐着贼难受吗？
But don't you find the car
quite uncomfortable?

535
00:28:10,867 --> 00:28:12,900
我不觉得啊！一点也不。
I don't! No.

536
00:28:12,933 --> 00:28:17,967
在那之前我开过一辆540，
装的是那种雷卡罗（Recaro）桶椅，
